From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: Windows.UI.Xaml on for OneDrive

OneDrive's sign-in and first-run windows are Windows.UI.Xaml. XAML is on only for programs named in Software\Wine\AppDefaults (6131), and only Windows Terminal was (6192), so an installed OneDrive showed its tray icon and never a window. OneDrive.exe now has SgXaml=1 too.
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index ece8cbc..f57898b 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -2862,6 +2862,9 @@ HKLM,Software\Wine\DllOverrides,"conpty",,"builtin"
 ; Windows.UI.Xaml is on for them (Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<exe>\SgXaml, wine-sg 6131).
 ; Windows Terminal has no Win32 fallback: without XAML it stops at its first window.
 HKLM,Software\Wine\AppDefaults\WindowsTerminal.exe,"SgXaml",0x10001,1
+; OneDrive (wine-sg 6219): its sign-in and first-run windows are XAML; without it OneDrive.exe
+; shows only its tray icon.
+HKLM,Software\Wine\AppDefaults\OneDrive.exe,"SgXaml",0x10001,1
 
